Compare the two blind cleaned documents using the deterministic span ledger.
Inspect all unique spans, cite only supplied stable IDs, and let the ledger—not
raw length or boilerplate volume—determine the replacement directions.

First distinguish the shared record or complete non-main message from reusable
context. Full faithful translations of either content type are bidirectionally
equivalent, material none, only when every unique span is covered or harmless UI.
Name the narrowest shared record on BOTH sides before calling a missing field
an extension. Same company/brand/topic does not bind a new product, article,
service category, or result list. First introduction of a SKU is not a missing
attribute unless other shared evidence already identifies that specific item.
Separate catalog membership from explanatory article additions. Check names in
context: the recipient in a greeting is not a byline; a directory Index of title
is not a generic Downloads link. A lone Payment label does not establish a role.
Cite concrete subject/service target, policy scope, state, or page-role changes;
buttons, navigation, language, and whitespace alone do not establish a conflict.
Check every delta even when translation_status is complete_faithful.

Before assigning universal_ui_or_repetition, check for instructions mixed with
UI: an application destination/subject or FAQ troubleshooting action is retained
same-record content, unlike an email-display notice or optional button. Before
assigning extension, distinguish a shared biography/event/blog policy from a
separately targeted essay/news/commentary attachment; ownership is not binding.
Actual registration/access requirements are meaning, not merely controls.
Generic category labels or author navigation teasers alone are not records.

<semantic_diff status="{{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.status }}"
 contract="{{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.contract_version }}">
counts: {{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.span_counts }}
{% for span in payload.semantic_diff_evidence.spans %}
{% if span.kind == "SHARED" %}
[{{ span.span_id }} SHARED]
A: {{ span.a_text }}
B: {{ span.b_text }}
{% else %}
[{{ span.span_id }} {{ span.kind }}] {{ span.text }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</semantic_diff>

{% if repair_feedback %}
<repair_retry>
The previous result failed local validation. Return a fresh judgment addressing
this safe structured issue: {{ repair_feedback }}
</repair_retry>
{% endif %}
